32813283-b1c0-4d52-85a4-7889eeff461c	fb9e2b49-d504-4495-a0ca-40b75cfcaafc	\N	LaaS_May_12.docx	The LaaS platform is currently anchored by the ai1 server, which serves as both the primary application host and a core compute node. It operates in tandem with the ai2 server to form a distributed compute fleet. At present, this dual-node configuration supports approximately 10 concurrent users. \n\nPerformance testing indicates that four simultaneous 4K video streams generate a network load of roughly 25 Mbps. Scaling this ecosystem to include the ai3, ai4, and ai5 nodes will require the integration of a lossless 10GbE switch and dedicated time for cluster configuration.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(Network Load Test)\n\n\n\nUn Resolved Issues:\n\nAn occasional driver-level hang in the NIC has been noted, requiring a hard reboot to restore network stack functionality. This is a known issue with specific Intel 2.5G controllers under heavy load and is being mitigated through kernel tuning.\n\nTrue Root Cause Unknow, (Suspect : Power spikes)\n\nIncident Occurred on March 08, and March 09\n\nRespective Logs can be found here:\n\njournalctl --since "2026-05-08 11:50:00" --until "2026-05-08 11:55:00"\n\njournalctl --since "2026-05-09 17:00:00" --until "2026-05-09 17:10:00"\n\nNote : These are in UTC time\n\n\n\n(Outage on March 8th)\n\n\n\n\n\n(Outage on March 9th)	{"confidence": 0.7, "keyInsights": ["The workload involves a distributed compute fleet with a focus on network performance.", "There are issues with network interface cards under heavy load, indicating a need for robust infrastructure.", "Scaling the system suggests a requirement for additional compute resources and network optimization."], "suggestions": "", "detectedGoal": "general_dev", "inputQuality": "sufficient", "fieldConfidence": {"goal": 0.8, "vram": 0.5, "intensity": 0.7}, "missingCategories": [], "detectedFrameworks": [], "datasetSizeCategory": "unknown", "estimatedVramNeedGb": 0, "estimatedComputeIntensity